WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:09.560
Which stretch of which chromosome travels with a trait in a family, and which gene

2
00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:11.020
inside it is broken?

3
00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:17.920
Before DNA markers, a human disease gene could usually be located only if its

4
00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:21.620
protein, or a nearby known gene, was already guessed.

5
00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:25.880
A gene known only from its effect had no handle.

6
00:00:26.733 --> 00:00:31.933
Collect families in which the trait segregates, with affected and unaffected

7
00:00:31.933 --> 00:00:37.653
members. Then read their DNA at variable markers spread across the genome.

8
00:00:38.633 --> 00:00:44.773
Each marker is typed in every family member, and tested for co-inheritance with the disease.

10
00:00:45.083 --> 00:00:49.003
The physical fact used is meiotic recombination.

11
00:00:49.943 --> 00:00:54.583
Markers close to the gene are rarely separated from it, so they travel with the

12
00:00:54.583 --> 00:00:59.323
trait. One percent recombination is called one centimorgan.

13
00:01:00.143 --> 00:01:04.963
A marker that follows the disease through the family, with few or no recombinants,

14
00:01:05.143 --> 00:01:06.683
is the signal of linkage.

15
00:01:07.617 --> 00:01:13.417
Examine more recombinant chromosomes, from more meioses, and the linked interval

16
00:01:13.417 --> 00:01:18.797
shrinks. Then find the genes in the interval, using techniques that identify

17
00:01:18.797 --> 00:01:21.677
expressed genes there, and search them for mutations.

18
00:01:23.137 --> 00:01:28.277
Proof is the same gene carrying mutations in affected people, ideally different ones

19
00:01:28.277 --> 00:01:31.297
in unrelated families, and the mutant protein tested.

20
00:01:32.167 --> 00:01:39.747
The LOD score is the base 10 log of a likelihood ratio: the probability of the data

21
00:01:39.747 --> 00:01:43.967
if the markers are linked, over the probability if they are unlinked.

22
00:01:45.227 --> 00:01:50.987
Idealised example: ten fully informative meioses, phase known, none recombinant,

23
00:01:51.367 --> 00:01:53.287
give a LOD of 3.01.

24
00:01:54.287 --> 00:01:56.967
Traditionally, above three is called significant.

25
00:01:57.927 --> 00:02:00.867
One recombinant in ten drops it to 1.6.

26
00:02:01.767 --> 00:02:04.747
A LOD of 3 is not proof.

27
00:02:05.607 --> 00:02:11.707
Since most loci are unlinked, it means odds of only about 20 to 1 for linkage, and

28
00:02:11.707 --> 00:02:17.007
will prove spurious in about one instance in 20, so replicate in independent

29
00:02:17.007 --> 00:02:23.227
families. And a linked interval holds many genes: the loop-tail interval of the

30
00:02:23.227 --> 00:02:26.407
mouse held at least 17 transcription units.

31
00:02:26.927 --> 00:02:29.487
So find a mutation in the gene itself.

32
00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:37.140
In 1983, Gusella and colleagues linked the Huntington disease gene to a marker on

33
00:02:37.140 --> 00:02:45.040
chromosome 4. In 1993 the collaborative group found an unstable, expanded CAG repeat

34
00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:52.220
in a new gene there, in all 75 families tested. A decade separated map from gene.

35
00:02:53.130 --> 00:03:01.280
In 1998, Beutler's group used 2,093 meioses to confine the mouse mutation behind LPS

36
00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:03.680
resistance to 0.9 centimorgan.

37
00:03:04.600 --> 00:03:09.460
Tlr4 carried a missense change in one strain, a null mutation in another.

38
00:03:10.220 --> 00:03:13.860
The method was needed because the gene was known only from its effect.

39
00:03:14.700 --> 00:03:21.920
In 2006, Cox, Woods and colleagues mapped inability to feel pain, in three

40
00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:25.460
consanguineous Pakistani families, to chromosome 2.

41
00:03:26.340 --> 00:03:31.980
They found three different homozygous truncating mutations in SCN9A.

42
00:03:33.100 --> 00:03:38.860
Mutant channels expressed in HEK293 cells gave currents no greater than background.

43
00:03:40.100 --> 00:03:45.820
Keep this rule: linkage finds a region; different mutations in unrelated families

44
00:03:45.820 --> 00:03:46.980
show which gene.
